Lab Material
Lab 2. Overcloud Architecture Overview
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will:

Understand the role and components of the overcloud in OpenStack.
Deploy and configure a basic overcloud environment.
Identify key components such as controller nodes, compute nodes, and network nodes.
Learn how the overcloud supports multi-tenancy.
Prerequisites
Before starting, ensure you have:

A machine with Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) 8/9 or CentOS Stream 8/9 installed.
OpenStack CLI tools (openstack-client) installed.
Podman installed (for containerized OpenStack services).
Sufficient system resources (at least 16GB RAM, 4 vCPUs, 50GB disk).
A working undercloud deployment (if following OpenStack TripleO methodology).
Lab Tasks
Task 1: Deploy and Configure the Overcloud
Subtask 1.1: Prepare the Overcloud Deployment Files
Create a deployment directory:
mkdir ~/overcloud-deploy && cd ~/overcloud-deploy
Generate a basic overcloud configuration template (using TripleO):
openstack overcloud deploy --templates \
--ntp-server pool.ntp.org \
--control-scale 1 \
--compute-scale 1 \
--network-scale 1
Expected Outcome: A deployment plan (overcloud.yaml) is generated.
Subtask 1.2: Deploy the Overcloud
Execute the deployment:
openstack overcloud deploy --templates \
--stack overcloud \
--libvirt-type kvm \
--overcloud-ssh-user heat-admin
Troubleshooting Tip: If deployment fails, check logs in /var/log/heat/.
Subtask 1.3: Verify Deployment
Check the stack status:
openstack stack list
Expected Outcome: The overcloud stack should be in CREATE_COMPLETE state.
Task 2: Identify Key Overcloud Components
Subtask 2.1: List Overcloud Nodes
Retrieve node details:
openstack server list
Expected Outcome: Lists controller, compute, and network nodes.
Subtask 2.2: Access Controller Node
SSH into the controller node:
ssh heat-admin@<controller-ip>
Verify OpenStack services:
sudo podman ps
Expected Outcome: Running containers for Nova, Neutron, Keystone, etc.
Subtask 2.3: Inspect Compute Node
SSH into a compute node:
ssh heat-admin@<compute-ip>
Check hypervisor status:
sudo podman exec -it nova_compute virsh list --all
Expected Outcome: Lists virtual machines (if any).
Task 3: Understand Multi-Tenancy in Overcloud
Subtask 3.1: Create Tenants (Projects)
Create two test tenants:
openstack project create tenant1
openstack project create tenant2
Subtask 3.2: Assign Users to Tenants
Create users and assign roles:
openstack user create --project tenant1 user1
openstack role add --user user1 --project tenant1 member
Subtask 3.3: Verify Isolation
As user1, list resources (ensure no access to tenant2):
OS_USERNAME=user1 OS_PASSWORD=password OS_PROJECT_NAME=tenant1 \
openstack server list
Expected Outcome: Empty list (unless resources are explicitly shared).
Conclusion
In this lab, you:
✔ Deployed and configured an OpenStack overcloud.
✔ Identified controller, compute, and network nodes.
✔ Explored multi-tenancy by creating isolated projects.

